      "content": "Sorry about the goblin tangent, I just can't help myself. Okay, focus, focus... flights!\n\nSo, you're considering switching terminals, eh? Well, it's a bit like navigating a goblin-infested cave - you never know what's lurking around the next corner. But, in this case, it's just about getting to the right terminal.\n\nTo decide if the flight from Terminal 2 is worth the trek, let's take a look at the airport map. It's a bit like a goblin's treasure map, full of twists and turns. You'll want to check the walking times and distances between the two terminals. If it's not too far, and you can make it within the 3-hour time frame, it might be worth the trip.\n\nBut, be warned, the airport can be a bit of a maze, even for a seasoned traveler. You don't want to end up like a lost goblin in a human city, wandering around for hours. So, make sure you have a clear plan, and don't be afraid to ask for help along the way.\n\nAlso, keep an eye on the flight departure boards and check-in screens to see if there are any updates on the Singapore Airlines flight",
